  {
    "pkattachmentId": 64014,
    "bookid": 64,
    "chapterId": 342,
    "fileId": 33484,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Clinicopathological features and differential diagnoses of T-cell&ndash;rich lymphoid proliferations (rT-LPs)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Werner Kempf",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Entities</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histopathological features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Phenotype</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Differential diagnoses</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Nodular rT-LP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mostly solitary reddish non-ulcerated nodule</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nodular or diffuse (in incisional biopsies) dermal infiltrate of small lymphocytes without significant nuclear atypia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Perifollicular accentuation or granulomatous component possible</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Admixture of a variable number of eosinophils, plasma cells and B&nbsp;cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD3+, CD4+ &gt; CD8+</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD8+ phenotype frequently in immunosuppressed patients (HIV infections with low CD4 counts, organ transplant recipients) and/or viral infections (herpes) or spirochaetal (lues) infections</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Primary cutaneous CD4+ small&nbsp;/ medium-sized T-cell lymphoproliferative disorder</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Primary cutaneous marginal zone lymphoma (MALT lymphoma) with high T-cell count</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Secondary cutaneous involvement in angioimmunoblastic T-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">In CD8+ rT-LP: Cutaneous CD8+ acral T-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mycosis fungoides&ndash;like rT-LP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Maculopapular eruptions, erythroderma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Superficial band-like or perivascular infiltrate of small lymphocytes and variable degree of interface changes (lichenoid pattern)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Intraepidermal lymphocytes can exhibit irregular nuclear contours</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD3+, CD4+ or CD8+</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD8+ phenotype can be seen in drug eruptions, immunosuppression, and syphilis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">In CD4+ rT-LP: Mycosis fungoides (CD4+); S&eacute;zary syndrome</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">In CD8+ rT-LP: Mycosis fungoides (CD8+); CD8+ aggressive epidermotropic cytotoxic T-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>CD30+ rT-LP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Maculopapular eruptions, papules, and small nodules</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nodular, perivascular or band-like infiltrate with medium-sized to (rarely) large lymphocytes, scattered or arranged in small clusters</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD3+, CD4+ or CD8+, CD30+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Lymphomatoid papulosis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mycosis fungoides with large cell transformation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Intravascular rT-LP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Context of inflammatory skin disorder or trauma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Large blastoid cells in and around lymphatics</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD3+, CD4+ or CD8+, CD30+/&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Intravascular T-cell and T/NK-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Angiomatoid rT-LP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Papule(s) or small nodule(s)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dense infiltrate of small lymphocytes, prominent proliferation of capillaries or postcapillary venules, admixture of plasma cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD3+, CD4+ &gt; CD8+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Haemangioendotheliomas, angiosarcoma with inflammation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Subcutaneous rT-LP</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 3.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Deep-seated nodule</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 191.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"255\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Subcutaneous infiltrates of small lymphocytes in a predominantly lobular pattern</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"189\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">CD3+, CD4+ or CD8+, &beta;F1+, CD30+/&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 200.05pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"267\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Subcutaneous panniculitis-like T-cell lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">MALT, mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue.</p>",
